---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocMock from '../../../components/DocMock.astro';

const headings = [
  { id: 'gating',            text: 'Free vs Premium' },
  { id: 'setup',             text: 'Setting up reminders' },
  { id: 'how-scheduling-works', text: 'How iOS scheduling works' },
  { id: 'per-bill',          text: 'Per-bill settings' },
  { id: 'per-subscription',  text: 'Per-subscription settings' },
  { id: 'custom-messages',   text: 'Custom messages' },
  { id: 'quiet-hours',       text: 'Quiet hours' },
  { id: 'savings-nudge',     text: 'Monthly savings nudge' },
  { id: 'not-arriving',      text: 'If notifications are not arriving' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Reminders"
  description="Configure bill and subscription reminders in BudgetBaby. How iOS notification scheduling works, per-bill and per-subscription overrides, custom messages, quiet hours, and the monthly savings nudge."
  canonical="/budgetbaby/docs/reminders"
  headings={headings}
>
  <div class="docs-content">
    <h1>Reminders</h1>
    <p class="docs-summary">
      BudgetBaby sends push notifications to remind you about upcoming bills and subscriptions. You
      control when they fire, what they say, and when they stay silent. The full Reminders surface
      is a Premium feature; the free plan still receives system-generated bill alerts but does not
      expose the configuration UI.
    </p>

    <h2 id="gating">Free vs Premium</h2>
    <p>
      The Reminders settings screen, including per-bill day overrides, custom messages, quiet
      hours, the savings nudge, and the weekly bill summary toggle, is part of the Premium
      feature set. On the free plan, BudgetBaby still creates bill records and you'll see them on
      the home and Bills screens, but the dedicated Reminders configuration page shows a Premium
      upsell instead of the controls described below.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Free.</strong> Bills are tracked in-app; you see them on the home and Bills screens. Reminder configuration is locked.</li>
      <li><strong>Premium.</strong> Full Reminders surface: multi-day offsets (1, 3, 7 days before), per-bill and per-subscription overrides, custom messages, quiet hours, weekly bill summary, monthly savings nudge.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="doc-tip">
      <strong>Day-zero "same day" reminders</strong> are enabled in the configuration alongside the
      multi-day options on Premium. Outside the Reminders screen, BudgetBaby does not push a
      separate same-day notification on the free plan.
    </div>

    <h2 id="setup">Setting up reminders</h2>
    <p>
      On Premium, go to <strong>Settings → Reminders</strong>. On your first visit, BudgetBaby
      requests notification permission from iOS if it hasn't already been granted, then saves a
      default configuration. The global settings apply to every bill and subscription unless you
      override them individually.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Default reminder days.</strong> Four options: same day (0), 1 day before, 3 days
        before, 7 days before. The factory default is <strong>1 day before</strong>. Multiple
        offsets can be enabled at once, for example, 7 days before plus same day fires twice per
        bill.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reminder time.</strong> The hour and minute at which all notifications fire.
        Default is 9:00 AM. Applies globally unless suppressed by quiet hours.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Weekly bill summary.</strong> An optional Monday morning digest listing all bills
        due in the coming week and their total. Useful for planning the week without opening the
        app.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="doc-tip">
      <strong>Notification permission.</strong> If you denied notification permission during
      onboarding or in iOS Settings, BudgetBaby cannot send any reminders. To re-enable: iOS
      Settings → BudgetBaby → Notifications → Allow Notifications. Make sure Alerts and Banners are
      also enabled.
    </div>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Settings. Reminders" caption="Global defaults apply to every bill unless individually overridden.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Settings</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Reminders</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-section-label">Default reminder days</div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Same day (day 0)</span><span class="dm-toggle"></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">1 day before</span><span class="dm-toggle on"></span></div>
