    <h2 id="how-scheduling-works">How iOS notification scheduling works</h2>
    <p>
      BudgetBaby uses local notifications, not server-sent push. They're scheduled entirely on your
      device and fire based on a date and time you set. They work without an internet connection
      and without our servers.
    </p>
    <p>When you save a reminder configuration, BudgetBaby:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Cancels all previously scheduled bill and subscription notifications.</li>
      <li>Calculates the next due date for each active bill and subscription.</li>
      <li>Schedules a notification for each combination of bill/subscription and selected
      day-before offset, at the global reminder time.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      This happens synchronously when you tap Save. The notifications are then registered with
      iOS and will fire even if the app is closed or has been force-quit, as long as notification
      permission is still granted.
    </p>
    <h3>Why notifications might fire at the wrong time</h3>
    <p>
      iOS has several mechanisms that delay or suppress notifications independent of what
      BudgetBaby schedules. If a notification fires late or not at all:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Low Power Mode.</strong> iOS can defer non-critical notifications when the battery is low.</li>
      <li><strong>Focus modes.</strong> Active Focus modes (Do Not Disturb, Sleep, Work, etc.) can hold notifications until the Focus ends.</li>
      <li><strong>Scheduled Summary.</strong> iOS 15+ can group notifications into a delivery summary. Apps in your summary list are batched, not delivered immediately.</li>
      <li><strong>App not opened recently.</strong> Local notifications are scheduled when the configuration is saved. If you've added bills since the last save, opening Settings → Reminders triggers a re-schedule.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Local notification" caption="Local notifications fire even with no internet, scheduled directly with iOS.">
        <div style="height:30px;"></div>
        <div class="dm-help" style="text-align:center; font-size:8px;">9:00 AM · Tuesday</div>
        <div class="dm-notif" style="margin-top:8px;">
          <span class="dm-notif-icon"></span>
          <div>
            <div class="dm-notif-app">BudgetBaby</div>
            <div class="dm-notif-title">Upcoming Bill</div>
            <div class="dm-notif-body">Rent due in 3 days, $1,200</div>
          </div>
          <span class="dm-notif-time">now</span>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-notif" style="margin-top:6px; opacity:0.85;">
          <span class="dm-notif-icon"></span>
          <div>
            <div class="dm-notif-app">BudgetBaby</div>
            <div class="dm-notif-title">Weekly bill summary</div>
            <div class="dm-notif-body">3 bills, $1,420 total this week.</div>
          </div>
