        </div>
        <div class="dm-help" style="margin-top:auto; text-align:center;">Scheduled on-device. No server, no internet required.</div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="per-bill">Per-bill settings</h2>
    <p>
      Below the global settings, the Per-Bill Settings section lists every active recurring bill.
      Tap any bill to expand it.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Day toggles.</strong> Enable or disable specific day offsets for this bill,
        overriding the global setting. For example, if your global setting is "1 day before," you
        can also enable "7 days before" on rent so you have a longer warning for the most important
        outflow.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Custom badge.</strong> Bills with an active override show a purple "Custom" badge
        on their card so you can see at a glance which bills have custom schedules.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reset to Default.</strong> Tap to remove the override and return the bill to the
        global schedule.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Saving a per-bill setting cancels the old notifications for that bill and schedules new ones.
      The change takes effect for the next upcoming occurrence.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Per-bill override" caption="Override day offsets per bill, purple Custom badge marks any override.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Reminders</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Rent</span><span class="dm-bar-action">Save</span></div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Rent</strong><span class="dm-pill purple">Custom</span></div>
          <div class="dm-kv muted"><span>$1,200 · 1st of each month</span><span></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-section-label">Reminder days for this bill</div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Same day</span><span class="dm-toggle on"></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">1 day before</span><span class="dm-toggle"></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">3 days before</span><span class="dm-toggle on"></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">7 days before</span><span class="dm-toggle on purple"></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-btn dm-btn-secondary">Reset to default</div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="per-subscription">Per-subscription settings</h2>
    <p>
      The Per-Subscription Settings section appears below per-bill when you have active
      subscriptions. It works identically to per-bill but applies to your tracked subscriptions.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Expand any subscription card to choose reminder days for that subscription specifically.</li>
      <li>The card subtitle shows the next billing date.</li>
      <li>Custom overrides display the purple "Custom" badge. Reset to Default clears the override.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Subscription billing dates can shift (trials, paused billing, plan changes). BudgetBaby uses
      the next-billing-date stored on each subscription record to calculate notification dates, so
      keep that field accurate when billing dates change.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Subscriptions" caption="Each subscription card shows its next billing date.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Reminders</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Subscriptions</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon star">N</span><span class="dm-row-label">Netflix<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Renews Mar 18 · $15.49</div></span><span class="dm-pill purple">Custom</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon star">S</span><span class="dm-row-label">Spotify Family<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Renews Mar 22 · $16.99</div></span><span class="dm-row-chevron"></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon star">A</span><span class="dm-row-label">Adobe CC<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Renews Apr 02 · $54.99</div></span><span class="dm-row-chevron"></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon star">i</span><span class="dm-row-label">iCloud+ 2TB<div class="dm-row-meta" style="font-size:8px;">Renews Apr 11 · $9.99</div></span><span class="dm-row-chevron"></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-help">Cards expand for per-subscription overrides.</div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="custom-messages">Custom messages</h2>
    <p>
      Inside any expanded bill or subscription card, a Custom Message field lets you write your own
      notification body for that bill or subscription.
    </p>
    <p>
      When the field is left empty, BudgetBaby auto-generates the body. The actual format the app
      uses today:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Bill, multi-day: title <em>"Upcoming Bill"</em>, body <em>"[name] due in [N] days, $X.XX"</em>.</li>
      <li>Bill, same day: title <em>"Bill Due Today"</em>, body includes name and amount.</li>
      <li>Subscription, same day: title <em>"Subscription Renews Today"</em>, body <em>"[name], $X.XX"</em>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you set a custom message, the body is replaced verbatim. Use it to add context the auto-generated text can't:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>"Check if we're still using this before it renews."</li>
      <li>"Transfer from savings to cover this payment."</li>
      <li>"Submit as a work expense before paying."</li>
      <li>"Decide whether to keep the annual plan this year."</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Custom message" caption="Your wording replaces the auto-generated body when the notification fires.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Reminders</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Adobe CC</span><span class="dm-bar-action">Save</span></div>
        <div class="dm-section-label">Custom message</div>
        <div class="dm-card" style="padding:9px 10px;">
          <div class="dm-help" style="font-size:9px; color:var(--text-primary); line-height:1.4;">Decide whether to keep the annual plan this year before the renewal pulls.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-help">Leave blank for auto: "Adobe CC due in 3 days, $54.99."</div>
        <div class="dm-section-label">Preview</div>
        <div class="dm-notif">
          <span class="dm-notif-icon"></span>
          <div>
            <div class="dm-notif-app">BudgetBaby</div>
            <div class="dm-notif-title">Upcoming Bill</div>
            <div class="dm-notif-body">Decide whether to keep the annual plan this year before the renewal pulls.</div>
          </div>
          <span class="dm-notif-time">9am</span>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="quiet-hours">Quiet hours</h2>
    <p>
      The Quiet Hours section in Settings → Reminders suppresses BudgetBaby notifications during a
      time window. This prevents reminders from waking you up or interrupting meetings.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Enable the <strong>Quiet Hours</strong> toggle.</li>
      <li>Set a <strong>From</strong> time, when the quiet window starts.</li>
      <li>Set an <strong>Until</strong> time, when the window ends.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Midnight wrap is handled correctly. A 10:00 PM to 8:00 AM window suppresses notifications
      from 10 PM until 8 AM the next day, including overnight. You don't need to set two windows.
    </p>
    <p>
      Notifications scheduled inside the quiet window are held and delivered when the window ends, they aren't cancelled. If your reminder time is 7:00 AM and your quiet window ends at 8:00
      AM, the notification fires at 8:00 AM.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-tip">
      <strong>Quiet hours vs iOS Do Not Disturb.</strong> They're separate systems. BudgetBaby's
      quiet hours suppress at the scheduling level, no notification is issued during the window.
      iOS Do Not Disturb receives the notification but silences the alert. Configure them
      consistently for the cleanest experience.
    </div>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Quiet hours" caption="Notifications inside the window are held until it ends, never lost.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Reminders</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Quiet hours</span><span class="dm-bar-action">Save</span></div>
        <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Quiet hours</span><span class="dm-toggle on purple"></span></div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>From</strong><span class="dm-time-box">10:00 PM</span></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Until</strong><span class="dm-time-box">8:00 AM</span></div>
          <div class="dm-kv-divider"></div>
          <div class="dm-kv muted"><span>Window length</span><span>10 hours</span></div>
          <div class="dm-kv muted"><span>Wraps midnight</span><span class="green">Yes</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-help">Notifications scheduled inside this window deliver at 8:00 AM.</div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="savings-nudge">Monthly savings nudge</h2>
    <p>
      The Savings Reminders section sends one push per month reminding you to fund your savings
      goals.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Enable the <strong>Monthly savings nudge</strong> toggle.</li>
      <li>Use the day stepper to choose which day of the month (1-28) to receive the nudge.</li>
      <li>The notification fires at your global reminder time on that day.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The default day is 15 (mid-month). If you're paid at the start of the month, this is a
      halfway reminder to check whether you've moved money into goals yet. If you're paid on the
      15th, consider setting it to day 16 or 17 so it fires just after your paycheck lands.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-tip">
      <strong>No goals, no nudge.</strong> If you don't have an active savings goal, the nudge
      isn't sent even if the toggle is enabled. Create a goal in the Goals tab to activate it.
    </div>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Savings nudge" caption="Single mid-month push reminding you to fund your goals.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Reminders</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Savings</span><span class="dm-bar-action">Save</span></div>
        <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Monthly savings nudge</span><span class="dm-toggle on purple"></span></div>
        <div class="dm-card">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>Day of month</strong>
            <span class="dm-stepper"><span class="dm-stepper-btn">−</span><span class="dm-stepper-val">15</span><span class="dm-stepper-btn">+</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="dm-kv muted"><span>Range</span><span>1, 28</span></div>
          <div class="dm-kv"><span>Fires at</span><strong>9:00 AM</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-section-label">Active goals</div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon target">E</span><span class="dm-row-label">Emergency fund</span><span class="dm-row-meta">62%</span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-icon star">V</span><span class="dm-row-label">Vacation</span><span class="dm-row-meta">38%</span></div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>

    <h2 id="not-arriving">If notifications are not arriving</h2>
    <p>If you have configured reminders but aren't receiving notifications, work through these in order:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Check iOS notification permission.</strong> iOS Settings → BudgetBaby →
        Notifications. Ensure Allow Notifications is on and Alerts/Banners are enabled.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Check the BudgetBaby Reminders screen.</strong> Settings → Reminders. Confirm the
        right days are toggled and the time is what you expect.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Check Focus modes.</strong> iOS Settings → Focus. Ensure BudgetBaby is in the
        allowed-apps list of every active Focus.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Check Scheduled Summary.</strong> iOS Settings → Notifications → Scheduled Summary.
        If BudgetBaby is in the summary list, notifications are being batched. Move it out for
        immediate delivery.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Open the app to trigger rescheduling.</strong> If you haven't opened BudgetBaby in
        weeks, open Settings → Reminders and tap Save. Even with no changes, this re-schedules
        every notification with the latest data.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Contact support.</strong> If none of the above works, email
        <a href="mailto:support@babyblocks.io">support@babyblocks.io</a> with your iOS version, app
        version, and which notifications aren't arriving.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="doc-mocks-row">
      <DocMock label="Diagnostic checklist" caption="Walk this iOS-side checklist when reminders go silent.">
        <div class="dm-bar"><span class="dm-back">Settings</span><span class="dm-bar-title">Diagnostic</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="dm-list">
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">iOS notification permission</span><span style="color:#34D399; font-size:14px;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Reminder days enabled</span><span style="color:#34D399; font-size:14px;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Focus mode allows app</span><span style="color:#F87171; font-size:14px;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Not in Scheduled Summary</span><span style="color:#34D399; font-size:14px;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg></span></div>
          <div class="dm-row"><span class="dm-row-label">Reschedule on save</span><span style="color:#FBBF24; font-size:14px;">!</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="dm-card dm-card-warn">
          <div class="dm-kv"><strong>1 issue found</strong><span class="dm-pill orange">Focus</span></div>
          <div class="dm-help" style="color:#FDBA74;">Sleep Focus is blocking BudgetBaby. Add it to Allowed Apps.</div>
        </div>
      </DocMock>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
